\ Spitfire: the coastal patrol, flown in the Lysander as 614 Squadron flew
\ its patrols of the Forth from Grangemouth from June 1940. The mission
\ places its sightings, a convoy and a U-boat on the surface, each a group
\ of ships at sea; the pilot reports one by flying a whole circle round it,
\ within a mile of its centre and below 2,000 ft, and the patrol is done when
\ every sighting is reported and the Lysander has landed. The strip below
\ the panel counts the reports and names the last one, with the home
\ airfield's bearing and distance.

\ how near a sighting's centre and how low the aircraft must circle to report it: a mile, 2,000 ft
1609.34 constant report-range
609.6 constant report-height

\ the roving U-boat: the flight's seconds before it surfaces and the seconds it stays up, each drawn evenly between the two (estimates); its speed on the surface, 10 knots, the Type VIIC's cruising speed (Wikipedia, Type VII submarine); its turn under rudder, degrees a second (an estimate); how far ahead it looks for land, metres, and how often, seconds
[ 300 1200 ] constant surfacing-times
[ 1200 2400 ] constant surfaced-times
5.144 constant u-boat-speed
1 constant u-boat-turn-rate
800 constant u-boat-lookahead
10 constant u-boat-steer-interval

\ a time drawn evenly between the two of a pair
: drawn-between ( pair -- seconds ) | pair | pair first pair second pair first - random * + ;

\ whether a ground point is sea, with its region's coast in use
: sea-at? ( point -- flag ) | point | point use-water-near point first point 2 @i water-at? ;

\ whether a point lies off the coast: sea, sea all round it 400 m out, and land 2 km out in one of eight directions
: off-coast? ( point -- flag )
	| point |
	point sea-at? not if false exit then
	[ 0 45 90 135 180 225 270 315 ] to bearings
	bearings ( bearing | point bearing 0 0 400 placed sea-at? ) all? not if false exit then
	bearings ( bearing | point bearing 0 0 2000 placed sea-at? not ) any? ;

\ a random point off the coast within 6 km either side of the line from one landmark to another, drawn again until one is found, at most 500 times
: off-coast-point ( from-key to-key -- point )
	| from-key to-key |
	from-key landmark-ground to start
	to-key landmark-ground start v- to line
	line heading-of to course
	line v-length to length
	0 to tries
	begin
		start course random 2 * 1 - 6000 * 0 random length * placed to point
		++ tries
		point off-coast? tries 500 >= or not
	while repeat
	point ;

\ the heading nearest a wanted one, 15° at a time either way, with sea at the lookahead and halfway to it; the wanted one where none is
: clear-heading ( point wanted -- heading )
	| point wanted |
	wanted to chosen
	false to clear-found
	0 25 1 do k
		clear-found not if
			k 1+ 2 / round-down 15 * k 2 mod 0 = if -1 else 1 then * wanted + 360 + 360 mod to trial
			point trial 0 0 u-boat-lookahead placed sea-at? point trial 0 0 u-boat-lookahead 2 / placed sea-at? and if
				trial to chosen
				true to clear-found
			then
		then
	loop
	chosen ;

\ the roving U-boat's sighting: off the coast between two landmarks, on a clear heading, surfacing and diving at drawn times
: roving-sighting ( name from-key to-key -- sighting )
	| name from-key to-key |
	from-key to-key off-coast-point to centre
	centre random 360 * clear-heading to heading
	surfacing-times drawn-between to surfacing
	{ :name name :centre centre :ships [ [ :u-boat centre heading ] ] :reported false :swept 0 :last-bearing null
	  :roving true :heading heading :wanted heading :steer-clock 0 :surface-time surfacing :dive-time surfacing surfaced-times drawn-between + } ;

\ the mission's sightings as the flight keeps them, each { :name :centre :ships :reported :swept :last-bearing :roving }: the angle swept round the centre so far, degrees, and the bearing from it at the last step, null while out of reach; a row whose ships are :roving names the roving U-boat and the two landmarks it surfaces between
: patrol-sightings ( mission -- sightings )
	| mission |
	mission :patrol [ ] @or ( sighting |
		sighting spread to ships to centre to name
		ships :roving = if
			name centre spread roving-sighting
		else
			{ :name name :centre centre :ships ships :reported false :swept 0 :last-bearing null :roving false }
		then
	) map ;

\ whether a sighting is on the surface: a fixed one always, the roving U-boat between its surfacing and its diving
: surfaced? ( sighting -- flag )
	| sighting |
	sighting@roving not if true exit then
	:flight-time game@ to clock
	clock sighting@surface-time >= clock sighting@dive-time < and ;

\ the roving U-boat a step on: every steer interval it looks for a clear heading from the one it holds, turns toward it at its rate, and runs on at its speed
: steer-u-boat ( sighting elapsed -- )
	| sighting elapsed |
	sighting@steer-clock elapsed - to steer-clock
	steer-clock 0 <= if
		sighting sighting@centre sighting@heading clear-heading :wanted ! drop
		u-boat-steer-interval to steer-clock
	then
	sighting steer-clock :steer-clock ! drop
	u-boat-turn-rate elapsed * to most
	sighting@wanted sighting@heading - 540 + 360 mod 180 - most negate most clamp sighting@heading + 360 + 360 mod to heading
	sighting@centre heading 0 0 u-boat-speed elapsed * placed to centre
	sighting heading :heading ! centre :centre ! [ [ :u-boat centre heading ] ] :ships ! drop ;

\ the bearing of a point from an origin, degrees from north clockwise
: bearing-between ( origin point -- degrees )
	| origin point |
	point origin v- spread to dz drop to dx
	dx dz atan2 180 * PI / 360 + 360 mod ;

\ a step of the patrol, elapsed seconds on: the roving U-boat steered while on the surface; each sighting on the surface not yet reported, while the aircraft flies within reach of it, sweeps the bearing's change since the last step, the shorter way round; out of reach the sweep starts again; a sweep of a whole circle either way reports it, with the message
: patrol-step ( elapsed -- )
	| elapsed |
	:sightings game@ ( sighting | sighting@roving sighting surfaced? and ) filter ( sighting | sighting elapsed steer-u-boat ) each
	:sightings game@ ( sighting |
		sighting@reported not sighting surfaced? and if
			plane@position sighting@centre v- spread to dz drop to dx
			[ dx 0 dz ] v-length report-range < plane@position second report-height < and if
				sighting@centre plane@position bearing-between to bearing
				sighting@last-bearing null? not if
					bearing sighting@last-bearing - 540 + 360 mod 180 - sighting@swept + sighting swap :swept ! drop
				then
				sighting bearing :last-bearing ! drop
				sighting@swept abs 360 >= if
					sighting true :reported ! drop
					sighting@name "REPORTED: {0}" format say
					6 :message-left game!
				then
			else
				sighting 0 :swept ! null :last-bearing ! drop
			then
		then
	) each ;

\ whether every sighting is reported
: patrol-done? ( -- flag ) :sightings game@ ( sighting | sighting@reported ) all? ;

\ the ships of the sightings on the surface as crafts for the scene, each at sea level on its heading
: patrol-crafts ( -- crafts )
	[ ] to crafts
	:sightings game@ ( sighting | sighting surfaced? ) filter ( sighting |
		sighting@ships ( ship |
			ship spread to heading to place to kind
			crafts { :kind kind :position place :attitude heading heading-attitude :state :sailing :smoke [ ] } add-last! drop
		) each
	) each
	crafts ;

\ the strip below the panel: the reports made of the sightings, the last one's name, and the home airfield's bearing and distance
: draw-patrol-panel ( -- )
	436 to x
	:sightings game@ to sightings
	sightings ( sighting | sighting@reported ) filter to reported
	sightings size reported size "REPORTED {0} OF {1}" format to count-line
	x floor-top 4 + count-line 0xffe080 draw-text
	reported size 0 > if x floor-top 17 + reported last :name @ dial-ink draw-text then
	:base-field game@ landmark-ground plane@position v- spread to dz drop to dx
	[ dx 0 dz ] v-length 1609.34 / [ dx 0 dz ] heading-of :base-name game@ "{0} {1:03.0f} {2:.1f} MI" format to home-line
	x floor-top 30 + home-line dial-ink draw-text ;
